### Iteration 2 — Design Patterns (Revealing-Module + Strategy)
```js
// 🏁 Sprint 2  ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Sprint Goal: Prove pattern literacy by delivering a sortable table
// that decouples algorithm from context via the Strategy pattern.
//
// PBI-006: “As a user I can click a column header to sort ascending or
// descending without page reload.”
//
// REVEALING-MODULE keeps public surface minimal, while Strategy lets
// us swap sorting algorithms at runtime.

const SortTable = (function() {      // Revealing-Module pattern
  const strategies = {
    text: (a, b) => a.localeCompare(b),
    numeric: (a, b) => a - b
  };

  function sortBy(columnIndex, type = 'text', desc = false) {
    const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr')];
    rows.sort((rowA, rowB) => {
      const a = rowA.children[columnIndex].textContent;
      const b = rowB.children[columnIndex].textContent;
      return desc ? strategies[type](b, a) : strategies[type](a, b);
    });
    rows.forEach(r => r.parentElement.appendChild(r));
  }

  // Public API
  return { sortBy };
})();

// DOD: Runs on Chrome, Firefox, Safari; Lighthouse perf ≥ 90.
```
*Sprint Review:* QA confirmed we can inject a *custom* strategy later, e.g., date sorting, without touching module internals.

